<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lancia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lancia was the chief stronghold of the Astures on the plain of the river Esla, near modern León in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. Roman historians record that the legate Titus Carisius besieged and took it during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars">Cantabrian Wars</a> around 25 BCE, sparing the town so that it would stand as a monument to his victory. Excavations at Villasabariego have uncovered remains of the later Roman settlement.</p></div>
